      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The projection matrix $\\mathbf{P}$ onto the vector $\\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}$ satisfies the following equations:\n$\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = (-3, -2), \\begin{pmatrix} -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}.$\nThus, $\\mathbf{P} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -2 \\end{pmatrix}.$\nNow, to find its inverse, we need to find the determinant of $\\mathbf{P}$:\n$\\det \\mathbf{P} = (1)(-2) - (-2)(-3) = -8.$\nSince the determinant is nonzero, $\\mathbf{P}$ is invertible.\nUsing the formula for the inverse of a 2x2 matrix with determinant $d$:\n$\\mathbf{P}^{-1} = \\frac{1}{\\det \\mathbf{P}} \\begin{pmatrix} -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{-8} \\begin{pmatrix} -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1/4 & -1/4 \\\\ -3/8 & -1/8 \\end{pmatrix}.$\nSo, $\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 1/4 & -1/4 \\\\ -3/8 & -1/8 \\end{pmatrix}}$ is the inverse of $\\mathbf{P}.$",
